      "writtenOn": "2024-04-05T21:20:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I started implementing this for checking if there was pending work, and realized that that isn\u0027t a valid assert in the case where some runtime error occurs. We may end up collecting some draws and then have to abort. In the current code, the failed device may still be flushed to the recorder, but in the end we should correctly be leaving unflushed work in the device if nothing ever actually uses it.\n\nHowever, I realized what I can always assert for these unregistered scratch devices is that they go out of scope on the Recorder\u0027s thread and that the recorder hasn\u0027t been snapped since the device was created. I also added an assert in `Device::flushPendingWorkToRecorder` that if it\u0027s a scratch device, it\u0027s being flushed in the expected next recording.",
      "parentUuid": "e81ffaf5_0c15ba5c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "207bdc7d0e6e7f5953ddedac4e70597be5c01cc5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f227bb32_a65bb9c7",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Surface_Graphite.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-05T15:23:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this just here so that the scratch version can call this function passing in false? If so is better to make a private factory instead that takes this parameter so that we can keep usages of the public APIs contained to how we want them to be used?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "207bdc7d0e6e7f5953ddedac4e70597be5c01cc5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b470b675_eaaad42e",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Surface_Graphite.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-05T19:04:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This `Surface::Make` is not really public, though, that\u0027s `SkSurfaces::RenderTarget(recorder)`.  I am also working in subsequent CLs to move all internal uses of `::Make` to `::MakeScratch`. Once that\u0027s done then I think it makes more sense to have this `Make` be entirely private so that you can either get a scratch surface or a public `::RenderTarget` which our internal code shouldn\u0027t be using.\n\nIn the long term I\u0027d even like to get rid of `Surface::MakeScratch` and update the internal draw code to operate on Device by itself. Right now a Surface is always instantiated, so if we want full texture reuse for internal operations, we either need to allow surfaces to not be instantiated right away (I don\u0027t love that), or update all the internal code to use Device and wrap the Device in an SkCanvas.",
      "parentUuid": "f227bb32_a65bb9c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "207bdc7d0e6e7f5953ddedac4e70597be5c01cc5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7b1ef4e_ed7f75c1",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Surface_Graphite.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-05T19:55:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah I wasn\u0027t using public here in the sense of public to outside users. Just public in terms of the class itself. If these API calls are going to go away soon then we can live with this for now. But if they\u0027re going to hang around for a bit until we actually have time to do the refactor, I think its worth not have parameters in the main factory we don\u0027t actually want people to use.",
      "parentUuid": "b470b675_eaaad42e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 63
      },
